\f0\fs24 \cf0 Task 5: Network Traffic Analysis Using Wireshark\
\
Objective\
\
To capture live network packets and identify different network protocols using Wireshark.\
\
Tool Used\
\
Wireshark 4.6.9 on macOS.\
\
Procedure\
\
1. Installed Wireshark and configured packet-capture permissions.\
2. Started capturing traffic on the Wi-Fi network interface.\
3. Generated network traffic by browsing the internet.\
4. Captured and examined packets using Wireshark.\
5. Saved the packet capture as a .pcapng file.\
\
Protocols Identified\
\
1. TCP (Transmission Control Protocol): Provides reliable, ordered delivery of data between applications.\
2. UDP (User Datagram Protocol): Sends datagrams without establishing a connection.\
3. QUIC: A transport protocol used by modern internet applications.\
4. mDNS (Multicast DNS): Supports discovery of devices and services on a local network.\
\
Observation\
\
The capture contained multiple protocol types, including TCP, UDP, QUIC, and mDNS. The Wireshark packet list showed 255 packets and zero dropped packets at the time of the screenshot.\
\
Conclusion\
\
This task provided practical experience in capturing network traffic, examining packet details, and identifying protocols using Wireshark.\
\
Evidence\
\
* Task5_Wireshark_Capture.pcapng\
